      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When CPU and general load look fine, intermittent drops often point to lower-level issues like duplex mismatches or faulty cabling in the physical infrastructure. Random bursts of loss can also be indicative of buffer overflows occurring transiently within the switch or router hardware, even if the average CPU is low. Check the physical link status (errors, discards) on the interface connecting to the peer reported by the traceroute.",
      "source": "target",
